    "description": "A process obtained a handle to lsass.exe with access rights permitting memory reads (PROCESS_VM_READ). LSASS holds plaintext credentials, hashes, and Kerberos tickets in memory; non-security-tooling reads of LSASS are a high-fidelity indicator of credential theft, independent of the dumping tool used.",
